  "verbalization": "Spaglumic acid appears to interact with SN12K1 through a series of target relationships, with the most direct link being its interaction with Neutral alpha-glucosidase AB, which is targeted by Stecholide I. This suggests that Spaglumic acid may act as a modulator of the enzyme Neutral alpha-glucosidase AB, potentially influencing its activity and subsequently affecting SN12K1. The presence of multiple pathways connecting Spaglumic acid to SN12K1, including through Raji and Maplexin A, indicates a broader network of interactions, possibly involving different molecular mechanisms. These pathways highlight the potential for Spaglumic acid to influence SN12K1 through various intermediates, suggesting a complex, multi-step interaction that may involve enzyme inhibition or modulation. The integration of these pathways underscores the importance of considering the broader biological context in which Spaglumic acid operates, emphasizing its role in modulating metabolic processes through the targeting of these enzymes.",
